  "title": "Lerochol Autoinjector Approved by FDA: What Patients Should Know About the New Monthly Cholesterol Treatment",
  "summary": "The U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) has approved a new autoinjector option for Lerochol (lerodalcibep-liga), a once-monthly medicine used to lower LDL cholesterol in adults with hypercholesterolemia, including people with heterozygous familial hypercholesterolemia (HeFH). The approval gives patients another way to receive Lerochol, which was previously available as a pre-filled syringe. The new single-use autoinjector is designed to make self-administration simpler and faster. According",
